| id | disposition | situation (requirement terms) | expected behaviour |
|---|---|---|---|
| Get | `UNSPECIFIED` for the exact state/parameters not covered; otherwise per sub-situation below | The requirements only say "Get a connection from the pool" (DOC-5), pool-full waiting (DOC-4), idle-timeout discard (DOC-2), ping-invalid discard (DOC-3). They name no per-state policy, no error signalling, and no behaviour after Release beyond DOC-12 declaring `ErrClosed`. Sub-situations: (a) `Open_IdleAvailable`; (b) `Open_NoIdle_BelowCap`; (c) `Open_NoIdle_AtCap`; (d) `Open_Waiting_BelowCap` / `Open_Waiting_AtCap` / `Open_Waiting_IdleAvailable`; (e) `Closed`. | (a) `handle`: return an available connection; DOC-2 requires discarding if idle beyond IdleTimeout, DOC-3 requires discarding if ping reports invalid, so a connection that fails either check must be discarded before hand-over and the Get retried. (b)/(c) `handle`/`UNSPECIFIED`: no requirement states whether to create a new connection up to MaxCap (DOC-10) or to wait; DOC-4 only says waiting is supported when the pool is full — which of (b) vs (c) triggers creation vs waiting is `UNSPECIFIED`. (d) `defer (queued)` per DOC-4, but the requirements do not state queue fairness, boundedness, or what a waiter receives if a queued connection turns out invalid. (e) DOC-12 names `ErrClosed`, so `reject` with that declared signal — but DOC-12 is about the pool being closed, not specifically Get-after-Release, so mark `UNSPECIFIED` whether `reject` or `handle`-with-ErrClosed is the requirement; as-is text alone cannot settle it. No requirement mandates or forbids blocking under a lock, so reentrancy/reentrant-callback behaviour is `UNSPECIFIED` (open point). |
| Put | `handle` for a well-formed return while open; `UNSPECIFIED` for open-but-anomalous payloads; `reject` for `Closed` per DOC-12 only if the requirement is read that way | "Put the connection back when no longer in use" (DOC-6). Sub-situations: (a) `Open_IdleAvailable`; (b) `Open_IdleFull`; (c) `Open_Waiting_*` with a waiter present; (d) `Closed`; (e) nil payload (see UV-Conn-nil); (f) already-returned connection (UV-Put-dup); (g) foreign/never-borrowed connection (UV-Put-foreign). | (a) `handle`: store as idle (subject to MaxIdle, DOC-11) or hand to a waiter per DOC-4. (b) `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not say whether a returned connection beyond MaxIdle is closed/discarded or blocks; DOC-11 only bounds idle count. (c) `handle`: DOC-4 says waiting is supported, so the returned connection should reach a waiter; ordering/fairness `UNSPECIFIED`. (d) `UNSPECIFIED`: DOC-7/DOC-12 say the pool is destroyed/closed; whether a Put after Release is silently dropped, handled by closing the connection, or `reject`ed with `ErrClosed` is not stated. (e)–(g) `UNSPECIFIED` for Put: requirements say nothing about nil, duplicate, or foreign connections on Put; the catalogue's observed nil-check and absence of origin/duplicate checks are as-is, not requirements. A `handle`-by-storing is not justified by requirement text for (f)/(g). |
| Close | `handle` for a well-formed single close while open; `UNSPECIFIED` for anomalous payloads and for `Closed` | "Close 关闭单条连接" contract text; DOC-2/DOC-3 require the pool itself to close/discard idle-expired and ping-invalid connections, but the Close event is caller-driven single-connection close. Sub-situations: (a) any open state; (b) `Closed`; (c) nil payload (UV-Conn-nil); (d) already-closed (UV-Close-dup); (e) foreign (UV-Close-foreign). | (a) `handle`: invoke the configured Close function on the connection and free capacity per DOC-10 (maximum concurrent live connections). (b) `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not state Close-after-Release; DOC-12 (`ErrClosed`) is the only closed-pool signal named, and whether it applies to Close is not stated. (c)–(e) `UNSPECIFIED`: requirements say nothing about nil/duplicate/foreign connections; catalogued nil-check and absence of origin/duplicate checks are as-is only. Requirement does not say whether closing a connection that is currently idle in the pool must also remove it from the idle set — open point. |
| Ping | `handle` when ping is configured and the connection is valid; `UNSPECIFIED` otherwise | DOC-3: "Support user setting `ping` method, used to check connectivity; invalid connection will be discarded." Ping is not in the Pool interface (catalogue). Sub-situations: (a) ping configured, valid; (b) ping configured, invalid; (c) ping not configured; (d) nil payload; (e) `Closed`. | (a) `handle`: report valid; no state change required. (b) `handle`: invalid connections must be discarded per DOC-3 — the pool must close/discard, freeing capacity. (c) `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not say what Ping does with no ping configured (error? valid-by-default?); must not be asserted from as-is text. (d)/(e) `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not address nil or ping-after-Release. DOC-3 also does not say whether Ping is only internal or also callable externally; catalogue says same-package only — as-is. |
| Release | `handle`/`transition → Closed` for the open case; `UNSPECIFIED` for repeated Release | DOC-7: "Release all connections ... when resources need to be destroyed"; DOC-12: `ErrClosed` means the pool has been closed. Sub-situations: (a) any open state with idle connections; (b) open with borrowed connections outstanding; (c) `Closed` (second Release); (d) open with waiters queued. | (a) `transition → Closed` and close all pooled idle connections (DOC-7). (b) `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not say whether Release must drain/close borrowed connections, wait for them, or leave them to callers (catalogue notes absence of borrowed-connection tracking as-is). (c) `UNSPECIFIED`: catalogue notes second Release is "the cell Closed times Release", but the requirement text does not state whether a second Release is idempotent, `reject`s with `ErrClosed`, or is a no-op — cannot be settled from DOC-7/DOC-12 alone. (d) `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not say what happens to queued waiters on Release (error them, leave them blocked, etc.). |
| Len | `handle` | DOC-8: "number of connections currently in the pool"; DOC-13 mentions channels. Sub-situations: (a) open; (b) `Closed`. | (a) `handle`: return a count consistent with DOC-8; requirement does not define whether "in the pool" means idle-only or idle+in-use — `UNSPECIFIED` on that definitional point, but the event itself is handled (no state change). (b) `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not state what Len returns after Release (zero? error? undefined?). Must not assert as-is. |
| UV-Conn-nil | `reject` if the requirement is read as declared refusal; otherwise `UNSPECIFIED` | A nil connection offered to Put or Close. Requirements say nothing about nil: DOC-1 says the connection type is `interface{}` (so nil is representable), and no requirement states an obligation to check. | `UNSPECIFIED` in requirement terms. The catalogue says nil is explicitly rejected in code (as-is), but no requirement or contract text (contracts are only doc comments naming methods/config) declares a refusal signal for nil. A blind pass must record this as `UNSPECIFIED` unless the nil-check is treated as a declared refusal — flag as open point. |
| UV-Put-dup | `UNSPECIFIED` | The same connection offered to Put twice. Requirements: DOC-6 says return the connection when no longer in use; nothing about duplicate return. No origin/duplicate/borrowed tracking is required anywhere in the doctrine. | `UNSPECIFIED`. Requirement neither mandates detection nor forbids it; no declared refusal signal exists for duplicates. Requirement does not say whether the pool must be robust to double return (capacity inflation, double hand-out) — open point. |
| UV-Close-dup | `UNSPECIFIED` | Same connection passed to Close twice. DOC-2/DOC-3 require the pool to close/discard on expiry/ping-invalid; nothing about caller double-close. | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not address duplicate close; no duplicate tracking is required by doctrine; no refusal signal declared. |
| UV-Put-foreign | `UNSPECIFIED` | A connection not created by this pool's Factory, or never borrowed, offered to Put. DOC-1 makes connection type `interface{}` (generic), but no requirement states an origin/belonging check. | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not require origin validation and declares no refusal signal. Whether the pool should accept, ignore, or reject is unstated — open point. |
| UV-Close-foreign | `UNSPECIFIED` | Foreign connection offered to Close. Same as above. | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not require origin validation for Close; no declared refusal signal. |
