| P-01b | `UNSPECIFIED` | Release completes before Put starts; Put arrives at `Closed`. | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not state whether Put after Release is a no-op, a close-the-connection, or `reject` with `ErrClosed` (DOC-12 is the only closed-pool signal). Ordering guarantee between Release's close of pooled connections and the in-flight Put is unstated. |
| P-02a | `UNSPECIFIED` | A Get is queued (DOC-4 waiting) then Release starts. | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not say what happens to queued waiters when Release destroys the pool (release them with error, leave blocked, or serve then close). DOC-4 only says waiting is supported. |
| P-02b | `UNSPECIFIED` | Release completes, then a Get whose first look predates it (at capacity). | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not say whether such a Get must observe `Closed` (DOC-12) and `reject` with `ErrClosed`, or whether a Get whose snapshot predates Release may still get a connection. No ordering/atomicity requirement is stated. |
| P-03a | `UNSPECIFIED` | A Get is queued; another caller Closes a borrowed connection (freeing capacity). | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not state whether a waiting Get must be woken when capacity frees (from a Close), or whether it only wakes on Put/creation. DOC-4 says waiting is supported but gives no wake-up rule. |
| P-03b | `UNSPECIFIED` | Close completes, then a Get at capacity. | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not state whether freeing capacity by Close makes a subsequent Get succeed (create new connection) or wait; DOC-10 bounds MaxCap but does not specify allocation policy. |
| P-04a | `UNSPECIFIED` | Get finds idle channel empty, Put stores a connection, then Get takes its lock; does Get see the new connection or create one? | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirements (DOC-4/DOC-5/DOC-6) state neither a visibility/memory-ordering guarantee nor whether a Get racing with Put must observe the newly stored idle connection. As-is lock discipline is not requirement text. |
| P-04b | `UNSPECIFIED` | Put stores a connection before Get looks; Get takes it. | `UNSPECIFIED` beyond: Put `handle`, Get `handle` (DOC-5/DOC-6). Requirement does not forbid or mandate the interleaving outcome; no guarantee that the stored connection is preferred over creating a new one is stated. |
| P-05a | `UNSPECIFIED` | The same connection is Put then Closed by two holders (contradictory). | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not address same-connection Put-then-Close; no borrowed-connection tracking, no duplicate/origin requirement, no declared refusal. Whether pool must close once, twice, or detect the contradiction is unstated — open point. |
| P-05b | `UNSPECIFIED` | The same connection is Closed then Put (contradictory). | `UNSPECIFIED`: same as P-05a; requirement gives no rule. In particular it does not say a Put of an already-closed connection must be `reject`ed or must not be stored as idle (storing a dead connection would violate DOC-2/DOC-3 spirit of avoiding invalid connections, but that is discarding-on-Get, not a Put-side rule). |
| P-06a | `UNSPECIFIED` | Get (ping configured) has read the ping field when Release runs; does Get follow DOC-3 discard rule after Release? | `UNSPECIFIED`: requirement does not state whether Release invalidating the pool must abort in-flight Gets, nor whether a Get already past the closed-check must still honour DOC-3 discard. No cancellation requirement exists (catalogue notes cancellation absent as-is). |
